  READING IT.  Choupo and NanoFiltran agree with each other to 1e-6 on
  the same inputs (the paper's line is NanoFiltran at 20 nodes and TOL
  1e-4, hence the third decimal), so every difference from the symbols is
  the MODEL's, not the solver's.  The model follows the trends -- the dye
  drives Cl- strongly negative (Donnan: the excluded trivalent anion at
  the wall pushes chloride through), and both rejections fall with
  chloride as the fitted charge c_X is screened -- and misses in two
  places, both visible in the paper's own figure: at 4 mol/m3 of dye it
  under-predicts the rejection of BOTH ions by 0.01-0.11 (the Cl- symbols
  sit above the line), and at the lowest chloride with 37 mol/m3 of dye
  it does not reach the measured -2.09 (it gives -1.82; Bowen & Mohammad's
  own model, the dotted line, does).  Root-mean-square over the twenty
  symbols: 0.077 in R_obs.  The CHARGE and the FLUX were fitted by Bowen &
  Mohammad to these data, so the residual is the pore model's at its
  fitted inputs, not a prediction error.
